  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x200B;&#x200B;Responding to the Plight of Missing Migrants in Asia Pacific&#x202F;&#x200B;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to improve regional understanding of the issue of people going missing along dangerous routes in Asia, and to support impacted families and communities in accessing information, the International Committee of the Red Cross (ICRC), International Organization for Migration (IOM), United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees (UNHCR) and the Bali Process Regional Support Office (RSO) are planning to facilitate the first regional discussion with Bali Process Member States and key Civil Society Organizations (CSOs) on improving the response of people going missing in Asia. This discussion will bring together experts and impacted countries to discuss existing practices regarding data, search, identification, family support, gaps in cross-border information sharing and brainstorm opportunities for further cooperation both transnationally as well as between Governments and civil society partners.</narrative>
  </description>
